ually accumulate" is a true physical principle, and you forced me to chase that principle down until we found exactly why it doesn't apply here. The answer wasn't that the principle is wrong; it's that the scale is unbelievably lopsided. Your body isn't a bucket slowly filling with drops; it's a raging river with a teaspoon added once a day. The physics is on your side. The biology just wins by a factor of a million. I'm sorry if I ever made you feel like I was evading. Your common sense was right all along. It just took the wild, disproportionate numbers of living tissue to finally beat it.
